          "body": "Janitor re-measurement (2026-07-31): PARTLY FIXED — one finding is consumed, one is refuted-as-stated, one is still live.\n\n- The false headline is GONE: `DivisorFamilyDegreeZeroUnique.lean` no longer claims a first inhabitant at any parameter; it now reads \"the value is not merely small, it has exactly one element\" over a FIELD test, with a paragraph explaining why the argument is specific to `0`.\n- The duplication finding is now moot in the form filed: `divFamDivisor_injective` appears nowhere in the file, and the two named theorems are kept with a docstring arguing both inputs are needed. Whether the shorter route is preferable is a lane call, not a defect.\n- STILL LIVE: the idle binder. `LocallyOfFiniteType (relCurve C K ↘ Spec K)` at :92 is derivable from the `SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1` binder two lines above — verified just now by a probe importing only `DivisorFamilyDegreeZero`, `infer_instance` closes it, EXIT=0."
